I'm playing a still-ascendable level-12 wizard, but it'll be a bit 
harder after a particular mistake...

I'd stashed all my spellbooks in the (co-aligned) minetown temple, along 
with anything else I didn't want to carry with me.

Deciding my AC was too high, I jebgr n phefrq fpebyy bs trabpvqr and 
summoned four silver dragons inside the temple, figuring that they 
wouldn't attack me. I now know better; it seems that enemies are happy 
to use ranged attacks inside temples. Furthermore, I had neither cold 
resistance nor reflection. Even then, I wasn't in any /great/ danger; I 
could still run away.

I fought for a brief while, but was quickly forced to run. With my ring 
of regeneration on, I started fighting the dragons individually, but 
they were still too strong in melee outside of the temple. Instead, I 
backed away and started casting expert-level fireballs.

I remembered, too late, that one of the dragons had picked up my entire 
stash of spellbooks...


